<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cockatrice_deck version="1">
    <deckname>Fungus v2 (2026-10-16)</deckname>
    <comments>Adopted 2026-10-16 after a 39-round screen (~1.06M games, scripts/deck_compare.py). Beats the
candidate-b base by -0.4697 +-0.0089 turns (std) / -0.5817 +-0.0105 (2hg), replicated across four
disjoint seed blocks (1340000/1350000/1370000/1380000) at ~50 sigma. 36 spells / 24 lands, mono-green
plus colourless acceleration.

USER RULINGS baked in (none of these is an agent decision): Doubling Season 3 (4 is OUT); Beastmaster
Ascension 4; Shroofus Sproutsire 1; Concordant Crossroads 1; Utopia Mycon 1; Saproling Migration 4;
Ancient Tomb 4; mono-green (black CLOSED); Mycoloth 0; Parallel Lives 0; Vitaspore out; Peat Bog out.

LEGALITY: Vintage/Legacy copy counts. Sol Ring 1 (Vintage-restricted); every nonbasic land capped at
4. Ancient Tomb is not Modern-legal, which is already true of Sol Ring.

MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED, for anyone revisiting a count: Saproling Migration 4 is the one edit clearing
the apparatus floor (4-&gt;3 costs +0.0061 std / +0.0088 2hg) and it is robust to the known EvalCard
token under-valuation, which can only reinforce it. A Wild Growth is worth THE SAME as a Forest
(-0.0036 +-0.0029 std / -0.0031 +-0.0032 2hg over two blocks), so the 3rd copy is not a ramp bet the
screen can second-guess. Hickory Woodlot BEATS Forest by ~0.018/copy in both formats, so its count is
pinned by the nonbasic-4 cap rather than by measurement. 24 lands is right: 25 is worse
(+0.0072/+0.0092) and 23 gains only in std. Every other single-card change sits at or under the
provisional floor (0.0068-0.0079).

HISTORY: the predecessor is archived at v1-sporesower-shelldweller/ with its own profile, value
sidecar and keep table (all three were fitted to that list and must never be read by this one). The
unadopted user variant stays at candidate-b-2026-09/. Full screen record:
docs/design/fungus-screen-2026-10-13.md and docs/design/analysis-Fungus.md.</comments>
    <zone name="main">
